      "title": "Latest quarter",
      "description": "Federal Reserve Z.1, series FL663067003: broker-dealer receivables due from customers (margin loans AND OTHER receivables). This is NOT FINRA's margin debt and must not be read as it -- at 2026:Q2 it is $742bn against FINRA's $1,502bn, about 49%, and the ratio drifts rather than being a scalar. The Fed's 'Security brokers and dealers' is a national-accounts sector, so lending booked in bank-affiliated entities sits elsewhere in Z.1. Quarterly and published about ten weeks after quarter end, so it describes a quarter already over: a regime measure, never a timing one.",
      "gridPos": {
